# The game options OpenHOI3's enhanced mode adds, on the Game tab below the autosave interval.
#
# Read by OpenHOI3 alone, and only in its enhanced mode: the original never opens interface/openhoi/, and has no code
# that would make a window of this name if it did. See docs/openhoi/README.md.
#
# OpenHOI3 makes the window below as a part of menu_settings_GAME (interface/settings.gui), so every position here
# is measured from that tab's corner. It finds the elements by their names, which must stay as they are; where they
# stand, their fonts and their sprites are the mod's to change. Each row is the autosave row of settings.gui over
# again, 46 pixels further down:
#
#   openhoi_<row>_label              the row's name; its text is a localisation key (localisation/openhoi_options.csv)
#   openhoi_<row>_value              what is chosen; written by the engine, from the OPENHOI_OPT_... keys
#   decrease_openhoi_<row>_button    the arrows that step the choice
#   increase_openhoi_<row>_button
#
# The rows: premonth (save before the month ends), timed (save on a timer), edge (scroll at the screen's edge),
# event (where event windows come up).

guiTypes = {
	windowType = {
		name = "openhoi_game_options"
		backGround=""
		position = { x= 0 y = 0 }
		size = { x=240 y = 320 }
		moveable = 0
		dontRender = ""
		horizontalBorder= ""
		verticalBorder= ""
		fullScreen = no

		# premonth
		instantTextBoxType={
			position = {x = 30 y = 96 }
			name = "openhoi_premonth_label"
			font = "Arial12_bold"
			borderSize = {x = 0 y = 0}
			maxWidth = 172
			maxHeight = 18
			text = "OPENHOI_OPT_PREMONTH"
			orientation = "UPPER_LEFT"
			format = centre
		}
		instantTextBoxType={
			position = {x = 30 y = 115 }
